# L §7.3: "correctly rounded to u, ties half-even": sqrt(2.25) = 1.5 exactly, a tie between 1 and 2 on the step 1,
# goes to the even 2.  1.5 is not on a cell edge of the step 1, so the value is widened to [r - u/2, r + u/2] =
# [1.5, 2.5]: bound 0.5.  "Composites are exact" on the rounded values and the bound "comes from interval
# arithmetic ... over the expression as written": 2 + 2 = 4 with [1.5, 2.5] + [1.5, 2.5] = [3, 5], bound 1.  "A
# printed result that rests on rounded transcendentals, with no round after them, prints ≈": round(2, 1, down) = 2
# prints plain.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input x225: num
def r: num = sqrt(x225) to 1 at reader
def r2: num = sqrt(x225) to 1 + sqrt(x225) to 1 at reader
def rr: num = round(sqrt(x225) to 1, 1, down) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  x225 = 2.25

ask a: r, r2, rr law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: (≈ 2 ± 0.5, ≈ 4 ± 1, 2)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
